# Project Structure Guide

This is a React + TypeScript + Vite project for HOMA, a Persian/Farsi furniture visualization app that allows users to upload photos and see how products look in their space.

## Key Files and Directories

- **Main Entry**: [src/main.tsx](mdc:src/main.tsx) - Application entry point
- **App Component**: [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) - Main application logic with step-based flow
- **Types**: [src/types/product.ts](mdc:src/types/product.ts) - Product and UTM parameter types
- **Components**: [src/components/](mdc:src/components/) - All React components
- **UI Components**: [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/) - Reusable UI components (Radix UI + shadcn/ui)
- **Utils**: [src/utils/](mdc:src/utils/) - Utility functions for AI processing, analytics, etc.
- **Styles**: [src/styles/globals.css](mdc:src/styles/globals.css) - Global CSS with Persian typography and HOMA brand colors
- **Config**: [vite.config.ts](mdc:vite.config.ts) - Vite configuration with path aliases

## Technology Stack

- **Frontend**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite
- **UI Library**: Radix UI + shadcn/ui components
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with custom Persian typography
- **Animation**: Framer Motion
- **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useEffect)
- **Build Tool**: Vite with SWC for fast compilation

## Development Environment

- Always use the virtual environment (venv) for Python dependencies
- Use `npm run dev` to start development server on port 3000
- Use `npm run build` to create production build